sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-006: Participant Profile Management — Profile Edit Sequence
    actor ProfileOwner as Participant
    participant UI as React Profile UI
    participant Firebase as Firebase Authentication
    participant API as Express Profile API
    participant DB as Supabase PostgreSQL

    ProfileOwner->>UI: Edit handle, role, institution, skills, portfolios, and contact
    UI->>UI: Validate fields and HTTPS portfolio URLs
    alt Client validation fails
        UI-->>ProfileOwner: Field errors with every entered value preserved
    else Client validation succeeds
        UI->>API: PUT /api/profiles/me with supported fields
        API->>Firebase: Verify token, MFA, active account, and PART role
        API->>API: Enforce owner identity and reject role or participant tampering
        API->>API: Validate canonical role, lengths, collections, and HTTPS URLs
        alt Invalid, cross-account, or duplicate handle
            API-->>UI: 400, 403, or 409 with field-safe details
            UI-->>ProfileOwner: Keep entered values and show errors
        else Valid owner update
            API->>DB: Upsert participant_profiles
            API->>DB: Delete and insert participant_skills
            API->>DB: Delete and insert participant_portfolios
            alt Persistence step fails
                DB--xAPI: Database error after zero or more writes
                API-->>UI: Server failure
                UI-->>ProfileOwner: Retry guidance with entered values preserved
            else All persistence steps succeed
                DB-->>API: Updated profile collections
                API-->>UI: 200 owner projection and success message
                UI-->>ProfileOwner: Render updated self-declared profile
            end
        end
    end

    Note over API,DB: Current discrepancy: the profile, skills, and portfolio replacement steps are not wrapped in one database transaction.

